event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","item_id":"rs_05e476cd00e87b1b016ac93f78b09c87d18f98c3bfb6d20d53","output_index":0,"sequence_number":116,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Implementing server-side rendering**\n\nI’m considering how to implement server-side rendering (SSR) for forms without relying on JavaScript in the browser. It’s an interesting challenge! I think I can use a basic app setup with HTML, CSS, and JS on the server side. I'll keep APIs minimal since they seem unnecessary. The forms should handle data trimming on the server, and I need to ensure that names are escaped. Also, stabilizing IDs is key, perhaps with an autoincrement feature in SQLite. I'll have to test it with a temporary database during requests and restarts."}

event: response.reasoning_summary_part.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","item_id":"rs_05e476cd00e87b1b016ac93f78b09c87d18f98c3bfb6d20d53","output_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Implementing server-side rendering**\n\nI’m considering how to implement server-side rendering (SSR) for forms without relying on JavaScript in the browser. It’s an interesting challenge! I think I can use a basic app setup with HTML, CSS, and JS on the server side. I'll keep APIs minimal since they seem unnecessary. The forms should handle data trimming on the server, and I need to ensure that names are escaped. Also, stabilizing IDs is key, perhaps with an autoincrement feature in SQLite. I'll have to test it with a temporary database during requests and restarts."},"sequence_number":117,"summary_index":0}

